[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. Circuit representation, ownership and DAE contracts

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Canonical IR (immutable circuit, device descriptors, analysis plans, sweeps) compiles into an immutable ExecutionPlan containing unknown ordering, CSC sparsity pattern, pre-bound device matrix slot indices, state layout, and signal catalog. No artificial 128-node or 256-unknown cap applies; size is bounded only by explicit caller resource budgets.

All analyses build on one modified-nodal DAE formulation:
F(x, t, p) + dQ(x, t, p)/dt = 0.

Devices stamp local F, Q, dF/dx, dQ/dx, and optional limiting/noise contributions into pre-bound CSC slots. DC solves ``F = 0``; AC solves ``(G + j*omega*C) dx = b``; TRAN solves ``F + alpha*Q + history = 0``; periodic/RF analyses reuse the same DAE evaluations and derivatives.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-STATE-001
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Session-local mutable state
STATEMENT: >>>
All mutable simulation, device trial/accepted state, and solver workspace shall belong to an explicit engine or run session; no mutable process-global circuit state shall be used.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Execute independent circuits concurrently across threads and compare against isolated serial runs.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-STATE-002
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Structural and numeric invalidation
STATEMENT: >>>
The compiler shall compute structural and numeric invalidation keys and invalidate affected sparsity patterns, symbolic/numeric factors, and operating points after relevant parameter or topology changes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Mutate numeric and structural parameters across reused runs and compare against fresh compilations.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-STATE-003
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Typed indices and bounded loading
STATEMENT: >>>
The core shall distinguish node, unknown, device, state, signal, and sparse-slot identifiers, validate all indices before allocation or access, and enforce caller-configured size, include, and hierarchy limits.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Run negative and boundary tests on malformed indices, deep hierarchy, and oversized inputs; assert classified errors without crashes or unbounded allocation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-EQ-001
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Analysis-independent universal DAE equations
STATEMENT: >>>
Every device shall expose residual F, charge/flux Q, and analytical derivatives dF/dx and dQ/dx independent of analysis drivers, using one documented SI sign, unit, and excitation convention.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Verify DC, AC, and transient equations for built-in and OSDI devices against analytic formulas and finite-difference derivative checks.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-EQ-002
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Central dimensioned convergence policy
STATEMENT: >>>
Newton control shall apply scaled dimensional residual and update checks, voltage limiting with consistent linearized corrections, bounded source/Gmin continuation with mandatory final physical Gmin removal, and finite-value checks; linear solver success alone shall never imply circuit convergence.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Test tiny-update/large-residual, singular, overflow, regularized, and multistable circuits and inspect convergence diagnostics.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-EQ-003
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Explicit initialization and tolerances
STATEMENT: >>>
Analyses shall distinguish operating-point initialization, NODESET hints, forced IC, and UIC modes explicitly and record effective dimensional tolerances in result provenance.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Compare precharged capacitor/inductor circuits across initialization modes against Xyce and analytic solutions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-EQ-004
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Transactional transient acceptance and rollback
STATEMENT: >>>
Transient integration shall commit trial device state, history, and events only after nonlinear convergence and LTE acceptance pass, and shall restore accepted state identically upon step rejection.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Force step rejections on nonlinear and history-dependent devices and verify identical trajectories to unrejected replays.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-EQ-005
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Breakpoints, events and sample semantics
STATEMENT: >>>
The transient engine shall schedule known source breakpoints, process model events with deterministic ordering, and distinguish accepted solver timepoints from resampled or interpolated outputs.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Exercise PULSE/PWL corners, switch transitions, and TSTART windows against analytic and Xyce references.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

