[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5. Public C ABI, .NET SDK, DSL and Strangler Fig compatibility

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-LANG-001
STATUS: Accepted
TITLE: C++20 core with language-neutral C ABI
STATEMENT: >>>
The core simulator engine shall be implemented in C++20 (CMake + vcpkg) for direct, low-overhead integration with SuiteSparse KLU, OSDI, and optional C/C++ numerical libraries, while exposing a flat versioned extern "C" ABI for C#, F#, CLI, and schematic clients.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Decision record (2026-11-20): V1 Rust prototype suffered high cross-language friction between its C# frontend, JSON-over-subprocess transport, and native C/C++ solver/model libraries. V2 adopts lean C++20 without Trilinos while keeping C#/.NET as the host SDK, StarLark-cs DSL, and schematic UI platform.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-004

