[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-DSL-002
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Hermetic budgets, parallel campaigns and behavioral separation
STATEMENT: >>>
StarLark-cs execution shall enforce step, wall-clock, cancellation, and memory budgets, use deterministic parallel_map/spawn futures for sweep/corner campaigns, and never run inside the C++20 Newton/device hot loop; runtime behavioral equations shall compile to the C++20 autodiff expression VM.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: Test budget exhaustion, deterministic parallel sweep ordering, and analytical B-source derivatives evaluated purely in C++.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
